      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Worlds already do this by forcing players into a chair with locomotion enabled and then implementing their own gravity. You'd rather do it that way anyways as well since you'll need to handle all the unique situations that presents manually, (such as readjusting the player rotation, etc) which isn't possible if you only relied on VRChat supplying a Vector3 to set gravity.\nCheck out Eccentric Rooms by suzuki_i for an example of using chairs to completely change players expectations on gravity.\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_32bfc2f2-724e-4875-ba56-0f2a175970b6",
